<title>USA: St Joseph hogs up $1.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>St Joseph hogs up $1.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>ST JOSEPH 1997-03-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA said compared with Monday, barrows and gilts were $1.00 higher. Top $51.00 per cwt.</p>
<p>The hog market got a jump start last week from the Taiwan news and prices have advanced over $5.00 in three trading days. This improved producers outlook. Slaughter was running eight percent under a year ago since the first of the year with cash market below a year ago. Hog and Pig Report Thursday may give a better insight for numbers. Interior Iowa only moved 100,000 Monday.</p>
<p>    US 1-3	230-270 lbs    50.50-51.00</p>
<p>    US 2-3	270-290 lbs    49.00-50.00</p>
<p>    US 2-4	290-310 lbs    47.00-48.00</p>
<p>Sows - up $1.50-2.00. Top $52.00.</p>
<p>    US 1-2	300-450 lbs    45.50</p>
<p>		    450-500 lbs    48.00</p>
<p>    US 1-3	500-550 lbs    50.00</p>
<p>		    550-700 lbs    51.00-52.00</p>
<p>    Boars:	300-700 lbs    42.00</p>
<p>		    200-300 lbs    43.00</p>
</text>
